{
  "description": "The shared cases of the revision sequence (revisions-design.md section 6 and decisions 3 to 7, 14 and 22; section 17). The engine's RevisionSequenceTests and the editor's parity test for model/revisionSequence.ts both read this file, so the two copies can't drift. Each named sequence has levels exactly as an entity's revisions block writes them (name, format letters or numbers, or values; first as a string for letters and an integer for numbers; skip, width, startEmpty) and the separator, always given here (a block without one uses \".\"). Every case names its sequence. A revision is text; \"\" is no revision. Groups: start, the revision a new object takes; isValue, whether a text is a value of the sequence, with its filled levels (parts) when it is; write, the text of filled levels; next, the revision after moving at a level (1 to 3), or refused at a list's end; chosen, whether a chosen name may be given when the item's latest revision is latest (ok, or why not: not-a-value when the sequence can't form it, not-later when it is equal or earlier); compare, the sign of comparing a with b (-1 a first, 0 equal, 1 b first), for values only; examples, a level's first five values on their own (all of a shorter list). A note says why where the reason is not plain.",
